  "verbalization": "Infliximab, a tumor necrosis factor (TNF) inhibitor, is linked to Psoriatic Arthritis through a series of indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Infliximab is associated with Ankylosing Spondylitis, which in turn is linked to Etanercept and Golimumab, both of which are TNF inhibitors. This indicates that Infliximab may share a common mechanism of action with these drugs, targeting TNF to reduce inflammation in autoimmune conditions. The presence of multiple pathways connecting Infliximab to Psoriatic Arthritis highlights the potential for repurposing Infliximab for this condition, as it aligns with the broader class of TNF inhibitors used in treating inflammatory arthritis. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Infliximab could be a viable treatment option for Psoriatic Arthritis, though further clinical validation is needed to confirm its efficacy and safety in this context.",
